WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:07.700
The high-water mark may already be behind
them, but the danger has far from subsided

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.250
on Sulawesi Island.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:14.919
At least 3000 people were forced to leave
their homes as rivers burst their banks and

00:00:14.919 --> 00:00:19.270
hillsides gave way under the heavy rains.

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:23.280
Flooding is hardly a rarity here during Monsoon
season.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:28.920
But still residents say they were caught unaware.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:33.960
The water started to rise here but then suddenly
a nearby river burst its banks.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:37.340
After 10 minutes the water was already 1.5
metres high.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:41.460
We didn't expect this at all.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:45.620
Emergency shelters have been erected in local
mosques.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:49.030
The military has been deployed throughout
the island.

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:57.510
Their first challenge: keeping evacuees warm
and fed.

00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:00.700
They're starving there, kids asking for milks
and food.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:04.129
It is hard to get there.

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:07.820
Rescuers continue to pull people from the
water throughout the island.

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:13.380
However with dozens missing and many villages
still underwater they warn that the number

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:20.799
of the dead will continue to rise.

